# fixedbugs, defect 569, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R2).
#
# SYMPTOM: a header whose own inline code converts a sign, as `gmp.h` does
# at its line 1882, was refused `ffi_header_refused` by the build's
# `-Werror=sign-conversion` before any binding was checked, on this Mac where
# Homebrew's `gmp.h` is found through `-I`; on Linux arm64, `/usr/include`
# being a system directory to clang, the same program built. GMP, libavutil,
# avcodec, avformat, swscale and libfdt were refused so.
#
# FIX: a group's header is included inside a region of its own
# (`emit/header_region.hero`): `-Wall` and `-Wsign-conversion` are ignored
# there, a missing return and an uninitialised read stay errors, and after
# it every check of a binding is raised again (`emit/checks_raised.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-569-a-library-s-own-sign-conversion-is-not-the-program-s.h"
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32
    function magnitude(x: i32) -> u32

function main()
    print(twice(x: 21))
    print(magnitude(x: -5))
